  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or loaded the page in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Forest:** A 260×260 ground plane carries 8,000 trees and 2,000 rocks. The trees are one instanced cylinder node for trunks and one instanced cone node for canopies. The rocks are one instanced sphere node, flattened and rotated. That makes three instanced draws.\n- **Placement and colour:** Positions come from a seeded RNG (seed 20240607), so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies get per-instance green HSL colours and rocks get per-instance grey-brown ones.\n- **Light and fog:** There is one directional light with shadows, plus a hemisphere light for fill. Fog is exponential at density 0.004.\n- **Camera:** An orbit camera looks at [0, 2, 0] from [0, 75, 115], with auto-rotate at 0.08 rad/s. The forest radius is 75, so it should stay fully in view. That framing is untested.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set in the first `onFrame` callback.\n\nThe structure follows recipe 2 in `docs/agents/recipes.md`.\n\n",
